{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6ffokceev","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM live bump silent drop root causes hardcoded player color and unknown sentinel","summary":"Runs 17-22 fired 0 live bumps despite the test-green Run-22 quota. TWO stacked causes, both invisible until Run-23's diagnostics: (1) agent._player_position/_bump_player_cells hardcoded player color 2 but the live ls20 board has NO color-2 cell (player renders {9,12}) so bump discovery no-oped silently; (2) after switching to program-derived color inference, the ls20 program renders non-player cells as the UNKNOWN sentinel and int(UNKNOWN) raising discarded the whole inferred set, falling back to {2} — caught live by the new bump_skip_reason='no player cell on live grid (player_colors=[2])' telemetry, fixed with a per-cell guard (skip UNKNOWN/non-int cells only), verified offline vs the real dev program + real live grid: colors [9,12]. Guards now in place: config_echo of effective knobs + player_colors in every run summary, bump_due/empty_batches + skip reason, regression tests through the REAL live_run AgentConfig constructor. Also: driver maps 'divergences' to reactive_turns (mislabeled counter) — run-22's divergences=24 at live 1.0 = 24 reactive turns, zero model misses. Run 23 itself was infra-dead: ARC API returned GAME_NOT_STARTED_ERROR on all 160 actions after a successful RESET (two consecutive launches); coverage note write 404'd transiently (endpoint 200 OK post-run). Rerun on a healthy ARC session expected to echo player_colors=[9,12] and fire first-class bumps from batch 1.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T13:57:36.156Z","vec":[-0.026909327134490013,-0.030950412154197693,0.005876466166228056,0.05772620067000389,0.13133014738559723,-0.013833069242537022,-0.014733686111867428,0.04526708275079727,-0.02817307971417904,0.04194309562444687,0.04437321424484253,-0.06476026773452759,0.08947122097015381,-0.03608327358961105,0.0005115229287